## 1. Deterministic Environment Readiness Gates (`PASS` / `FAIL`)

<!-- GEN: Binary CLI gates (exit 0 = PASS, exit != 0 = FAIL). An unready or conflicted environment that cannot be resolved reports BLOCKED (never counts as PASS). -->
| Readiness Gate | Command (`cwd: {{target_dir}}`) | Pass Criteria (`PASS` / `FAIL`) |
|---|---|---|
| **Port & Process Probe (`E2`)** | `{{probe_cmd}}` | `PASS` when ports are either free to start or healthy & reusable |
| **Revision & Local Schema Alignment (`E8`, `E9`)** | `{{revision_and_migrate_cmd}}` | `PASS` when checked-out SHA matches target and local DB migration exits `0` |
| **Service Health & Readiness (`E4`)** | `{{health_check_cmd}}` | `PASS` when all required health endpoints / readiness checks return ready within timeout |
| **Isolated Seed & Stub Readiness (`E5`–`E7`)** | `{{seed_and_stub_check_cmd}}` | `PASS` when local seed succeeds and active stubs respond with `stubbed: <provider>` recorded |

## 2. 6-Step Environment Lifecycle

1. **Probe first (`E2`)**: inspect `{{ports}}` — if running and healthy, reuse; if running, unhealthy, and unowned, report `BLOCKED` ([01]({{ref_01}})).
2. **Align revision & schema (`E8`, `E9`)**: bring owned services to the exact reviewed revision and migrate the local/disposable DB ([01]({{ref_01}})).
3. **Start missing services (`E1`, `E3`)**: start only missing services in the background with logs in `{{log_dir}}`, recording PIDs/containers you started ([01]({{ref_01}})).
4. **Verify readiness (`E4`)**: wait for all readiness gates (`PASS` / `FAIL`) before running any test case ([01]({{ref_01}}), [03]({{ref_03}})).
5. **Seed isolated data, accounts & stubs (`E5`–`E7`, `E10`, `E13`)**: load isolated fixtures, per-role accounts from config, and provider sandboxes or `stubbed: <provider>` mocks ([02]({{ref_02}})).
6. **Record & clean up (`E11`, `E12`, `E14`)**: attach the environment record to test evidence and stop/clean only what you created ([03]({{ref_03}})).

## 3. Never-List

- **Never** stop, restart, or reset a stack or service you did not start (`E2`).
- **Never** run `{{forbidden_data_commands}}` — they clone, reset, or overwrite shared data (`E5`).
- **Never** use production data or real user accounts, or print/paste secret credential values (`E5`, `E6`, `E13`).
- **Never** report a stubbed test result without the `stubbed: <provider>` label (`E7`).
- **Never** modify application code to work around an environment failure — report `BLOCKED` (`E12`).

## 4. Mandatory Rules (`E1`–`E14`)

| ID | Rule | Reference |
|---|---|---|
| **E1** | **Know the service topology** (services, ports, `cwd`, start order, health checks). | [01]({{ref_01}}) |
| **E2** | **Probe before starting; never stop what you did not start.** | [01]({{ref_01}}) |
| **E3** | **Start in the background, capture logs, and record process ownership.** | [01]({{ref_01}}) |
| **E4** | **Verify readiness with a bounded timeout before running tests.** | [01]({{ref_01}}), [03]({{ref_03}}) |
| **E5** | **Use isolated test data** (dedicated tenant/run IDs or local fixtures; never shared/prod data). | [02]({{ref_02}}) |
| **E6** | **Maintain per-role test accounts** referenced by config key only (never real users). | [02]({{ref_02}}) |
| **E7** | **External providers: sandbox first, or network-edge stub labelled `stubbed: <provider>`.** | [02]({{ref_02}}) |
| **E8** | **Migrate the local/disposable DB schema to the reviewed revision.** | [01]({{ref_01}}) |
| **E9** | **Run the exact reviewed revision** across owned services and record the commit SHA. | [01]({{ref_01}}) |
| **E10** | **Enforce the environment matrix** (logical in-app selectors vs. physical DB targets). | [02]({{ref_02}}) |
| **E11** | **Clean up created test data and stop only owned processes after the run.** | [03]({{ref_03}}) |
| **E12** | **Report `BLOCKED` on environment failure** — never work around via application code changes. | [03]({{ref_03}}) |
| **E13** | **Keep secrets local** — never echo, log, or paste credential values into reports. | [02]({{ref_02}}), [03]({{ref_03}}) |
| **E14** | **Record the complete environment block** alongside acceptance test evidence. | [03]({{ref_03}}) |

